        observe: "Count exceptions by type and origin in logs or metrics; a sudden rise in a single type after a deploy is one of the fastest regression signals.",
        security: "Do not return exception messages or stack traces to API clients; they reveal internals such as SQL, file paths, and library versions. Log them server-side with a correlation id.",
        checklist: ['Checked only for recoverable, caller-handleable conditions', 'Narrow catch blocks', 'No empty catch blocks', 'Interrupts restored or rethrown', 'UncheckedIOException in lambdas', 'No exceptions for normal control flow', 'Internals never leaked to clients'],
        sources: ['The Java Language Specification, chapter 11: exceptions', 'Bloch, "Effective Java" (3rd ed.), items 69–77', 'Venners, "The Trouble with Checked Exceptions: A Conversation with Anders Hejlsberg" (2003)'],
